I'm confident the single root cause is `search`. The reservation memory step doesn't reach users, so I'm not naming it.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, metric, count(*) AS n, avg(value) AS avg_ready, min(value) AS min_ready, max(value) AS max_ready FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric = 'k8s.container.ready' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'search%' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "The search pod's container-ready metric is 0 across every abnormal sample, so it never came back."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, metric, count(*) AS n, min(value) AS min_restarts, max(value) AS max_restarts FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric = 'k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'search%' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "The search pod restarted 3 to 6 times during the abnormal window, with restart counts climbing and never recovering."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'search' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "The search service emits no spans at all in the abnormal period, against 981 Server spans in normal."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) AS n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6, 0.95) AS p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name = 'search.Search/Nearby' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Frontend's calls to search.Search/Nearby fail fast (p95 about 0.02 ms) instead of taking about 9 ms as in normal."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code AS code, count(*) AS n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6, 0.95) AS p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name = 'HTTP /hotels' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Frontend's HTTP /hotels requests return 500 in 780 spans, all failing fast, versus 200 in normal."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, message, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE level = 'ERROR' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Frontend logs 1128 ERROR entries 'Search service failed' during the abnormal window; normal has almost none."}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

